{
    "background_story": "Kenzo was a skilled craftsman who valued simplicity and functionality above all else. Growing up in a family of modest means, he learned early on to make do with what he had and to fix things rather than replace them. As a result, Kenzo developed a keen eye for practical design and a talent for creating beautiful, yet functional pieces of furniture. He started a small workshop in his garage, where he spent his days building and repairing everything from tables to bicycles. Kenzo's practical approach to life earned him a loyal following among his friends and neighbors, who appreciated his no-nonsense attitude and his ability to create something useful from almost nothing. His motto, 'Form follows function,' guided his work and inspired others to adopt a more practical approach to life.",
